Cell[TextData[{
 "Code capacity and the phenomenological level are both quadratic in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],
 " and differ by a constant factor \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],
 " against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"10", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],
 ". The circuit-level curve is a different shape entirely, and the next \
section is about why."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One caveat on that figure, and it is the book's: \"A threshold in a \
phenomenological model should not be confused with the threshold derived from \
a full circuit model; they are not at all comparable\" (\[Section]10.4). The \
three curves share an axis but not a quantity \[LongDash] the \
phenomenological ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],
 " is a rate per qubit per round, the circuit-level ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],
 " a rate per location, and the phenomenological model ignores how many gates \
a syndrome bit costs. Read the picture as one code losing ground as \
assumptions are dropped, not as three thresholds being compared."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],

Cell["What circuit-level noise actually costs", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],

Cell["\<\
Two facts fall out of these polynomials that are hard to state without them. \
Both are about the extraction circuit rather than the code, and both are \
exact.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Duality is a property of the codes, not of the circuits that \
measure them.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The bit-flip and phase-flip codes are the same code with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],
 " exchanged; both are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],
 ", and under depolarizing noise at code capacity their rates are identical. \
At circuit level they are not:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"lead", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
      " ", "&"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"lead", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QECLogicalErrorRate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QECCode", "[", "\"\<BitFlipCode\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Circuit\>\"", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Rounds\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n",
      "     ", 
     RowBox[{"lead", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QECLogicalErrorRate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QECCode", "[", "\"\<PhaseFlipCode\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Circuit\>\"", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Rounds\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}],
   "\n", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[56]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"32", " ", "p"}], "15"], ",", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"112", " ", "p"}], "15"]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[56]= ",ExpressionUUID->"64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The asymmetry is entirely the rotations. The phase-flip code's generators \
are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],
 "-type, so its extraction needs eight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],
 " gates that the bit-flip code's does not, and each is a fresh depolarizing \
location sitting on a data qubit. Switch the one-qubit-gate noise off and the \
two codes agree again, to the coefficient:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"noise", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Circuit\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"<|", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\"\<TwoQubit\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<Measurement\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<Reset\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "p"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}],
      ",", "\n", "        ", 
     RowBox[{"lead", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}],
        " ", "&"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"lead", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QECLogicalErrorRate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QECCode", "[", "\"\<BitFlipCode\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "noise", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Rounds\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n",
      "     ", 
     RowBox[{"lead", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QECLogicalErrorRate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QECCode", "[", "\"\<PhaseFlipCode\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "noise", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Rounds\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}],
   "\n", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[57]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"32", " ", "p"}], "15"], ",", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"32", " ", "p"}], "15"]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[57]= ",ExpressionUUID->"70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["This extraction circuit stops a distance-three code correcting \
single faults.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The five-qubit code has distance 3, so at code capacity and at the \
phenomenological level its logical error rate starts at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],
 ": any one error is corrected. With this circuit it starts at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QECLogicalErrorRate", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QECCode", "[", "\"\<5QubitCode\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Circuit\>\"", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Rounds\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "    ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "\n", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[58]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FractionBox[
  RowBox[{"29", " ", "p"}], "5"]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[58]= ",ExpressionUUID->"3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note the phrasing: this is a defect of the ",
 StyleBox["gadget", "TI"],
 ", not a property of circuit-level noise. Gottesman's \[Section]10.2 exists \
precisely so that circuit noise need not cost the exponent \[LongDash] a \
gadget satisfying its propagation properties keeps a distance-three code at \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],
 " under circuit noise. Order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],
 " is the signature of a construction that does not satisfy them."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mechanism is the ",
 StyleBox["hook error", "TI"],
 ", and it is worth being exact about, because the direction of the CNOTs \
here is the mirror of figure 12.1b's and the obvious transcription is wrong. \
With the ancilla as target, an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],
 " on the ancilla reaches no data qubit at all \[LongDash] CNOT carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],
 " only from control to target, so it sits there and flips one readout. The \
fault that spreads is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],
 " (hence also a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],
 "): CNOT carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],
 " from target back to control, the ancilla keeps its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],
 ", and it lands on every data qubit the ladder has ",
 StyleBox["still to touch",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". After the un-rotation the residual is exactly the un-extracted tail of \
the generator \[LongDash] a mid-ladder ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],
 " on the five-qubit code's ",
 Cell[BoxData["XZZXI"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],
 " leaves ",
 Cell[BoxData["IZZXI"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["IIZXI"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData["IIIXI"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],
 " \[LongDash] and, being a sub-product of the generator, it does not fire \
that generator's own check in the round it happened. A ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 " before the first CNOT leaves the whole generator, which is a stabilizer \
and harmless; after the last, nothing. Only mid-ladder hurts."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],

Cell["\<\
Count what that does to the decoder's job. At the phenomenological level \
every single fault has its own detector signature, so no single fault is ever \
ambiguous. With this circuit the signatures collide, and some of the \
colliding faults do different things to the logical qubit \[LongDash] at \
which point no decoder reading detectors alone can tell them apart.\
