Cell["\<\
Nineteen faults, nineteen distinct signatures, none ambiguous \[LongDash] \
against 288 faults collapsing onto 71 signatures of which 29 carry \
conflicting logical effects. The code did not get worse; the circuit \
measuring it is not fault tolerant.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],

Cell["\<\
This is the gap that verified ancillas exist to close, and the book spends a \
chapter on it: cat states (\[Section]12.1.2\[Dash]12.1.3) feeding Shor error \
correction (\[Section]12.2), Steane error correction (\[Section]12.3), Knill \
error correction (\[Section]12.4), with \[Section]12.5 comparing their costs.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three of those are now built, and they close the gap in the direction the \
number above measures. ",
 Cell[BoxData["QECCatState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],
 " prepares and verifies the cat, with the set of checks derived rather than \
assumed. ",
 Cell[BoxData["QECPauliMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],
 " spends it on a transversal controlled-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 " and repeats with a majority vote (\[Section]12.1.4, Theorem 12.1); \
measuring the same generator the same circuit-level way, one fault now leaves \
at most ",
 StyleBox["one",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " data error where the bare ancilla leaves ",
 StyleBox["four",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["QECErrorCorrection"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],
 " is Steane EC, and it fills the slot between repetitions that Theorem 12.1 \
needs, chosen for the reason \[Section]12.3.3 gives: its ancilla and \
measurement errors enter additively, so it needs no repeated syndrome \
measurement at all."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two things are still missing, and both are named rather than implied. Shor \
and Knill EC are not built. And the encoded ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"|", "0"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"|", "+"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],
 " that Steane EC consumes are prepared here by the code's own \
non-fault-tolerant encoder, so the gadget is fault tolerant ",
 StyleBox["given a clean ancilla", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] which is precisely the part \[Section]12.3.1 calls \"the \
complicated part of Steane EC\" and defers to chapter 13. That cost is \
measured rather than waved at: a fault in the interaction leaves one data \
error, a fault in the preparation leaves up to four."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],

Cell["The next three sections are those gadgets from the outside.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],

Cell["Verified cat states", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A cat state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"|", "0"}], "\[Ellipsis]", "0", "\[RightAngleBracket]", "+", 
    RowBox[{"|", "1"}], "\[Ellipsis]", "1", "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],
 " is the ancilla that makes the controlled-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],
 " transversal: one ancilla qubit per letter of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],
 ", each touching one data qubit, so a single fault cannot reach several of \
them. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QECCatState", "[", "m", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],
 " gives the preparation circuit together with the parity checks that verify \
it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QECCatState", "[", "4", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Instructions\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
