}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Which pairs to check is the interesting question, and the book leaves the \
set open \[LongDash] \"if we do this on enough pairs of qubits, any single \
fault in the circuit originally constructing the cat state will be picked up \
by the checks\". Here it is derived instead, by propagating every single \
fault of the preparation and keeping the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],
 " patterns that matter. Two reductions make the set small: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"\[CircleTimes]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],
 " stabilises the cat, so a pattern and its complement are one error, and a \
canonical weight of one is a single data error, which the code corrects."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QECCatState", "[", "4", "]"}], "[", "\"\<DangerousPatterns\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[61]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[61]= ",ExpressionUUID->"64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
That single pattern is the book's own figure 12.3b, recovered rather than \
transcribed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<ChecksCoverQ\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],
 " is the proof obligation rather than a remark: a ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],
 " says the chosen pairs miss a dangerous pattern, which means the gadget is \
not fault tolerant. The count follows a rule the book does not state \
\[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],
 " checks suffice, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],
 " need none at all:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

