Cell[TextData[{
 "On the five-qubit code the same gate is not a gadget at all, and section \
11.4 says why in one direction: demanding that transversal CNOT preserve the \
stabilizer forces the generators to be ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ba8138a-66ce-478c-2957-8ad4137b2dd6"],
 "-only or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35c9e6d4-f3c4-84c1-63f6-ff918676ee2b"],
 "-only, which is the definition of a CSS code."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6fd66644-13e4-6fa7-15ee-782ea591358d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00abf1cf-696b-3507-30a8-e8a9081f9c6d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03d898fe-d35a-9eef-31e7-11bbe6ece435"],
 " and CNOT generate the Clifford group, so the seven-qubit code performs the \
",
 StyleBox["whole logical Clifford group transversally",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] with the caveat above, that each gate arrives conjugated. What \
is missing is everything outside that group: no transversal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03dda600-4b0b-c3af-31e2-386a6ebf91f5"],
 ", on this or any code of this kind, and that is chapter 13's problem rather \
than a gap in this one."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4de38b79-ee67-8bee-7b90-23228b13d934"],

Cell["Putting the gadgets together: FT(C)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"347cf1ed-0cc4-b4dc-5c03-e8b7a5761e26"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every gadget so far has been built and checked on its own. Definition 10.6 \
is the instruction for spending them all at once. Take an ideal circuit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d81b9ce-3a4c-aa2a-2bbe-30a8bffef970"],
 ", replace each of its qubits with a ",
 StyleBox["block",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of the code, replace each of its locations with the corresponding gadget, \
and after every preparation, gate and storage gadget put an ",
 StyleBox["error correction gadget",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on each block involved \[LongDash] never after a measurement gadget, \
because its output is classical and classical circuits are assumed not to \
fail."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6bb9b374-9caf-337d-1946-2b3e155b9e47"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QECFaultTolerant"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c340229-13f4-0181-15cb-a473a58153eb"],
 " is that substitution. Here is a four-location circuit \[LongDash] prepare \
two logical qubits, Hadamard one, CNOT them, measure both \[LongDash] made \
fault tolerant on the seven-qubit code:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25dfa134-0866-9bb5-53e4-397ea910e99f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QECFaultTolerant", "[", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<R\>\"", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<R\>\"", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<M\>\"", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<M\>\"", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
    "    ", 
    RowBox[{"QECCode", "[", "\"\<SteaneCode\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
  "[", "\"\<Gadgets\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[86]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"425139cc-45a5-cefb-726e-b0966c5194c1"],

