Cell["\<\
Two places where this note is deliberately outside the sources, and says so \
rather than implying cover it does not have. The exact circuit-level rate is \
a closed-form polynomial obtained by folding fault locations into a \
distribution over effects; \[Section]10.4 lists rigorous proof, simulation, \
analytical estimate and hybrid methods for getting at a threshold, and this \
is none of them. And the decoder optimises over the whole spacetime fault \
history, which is the strategy \[Section]12.2.2 raises and then sets aside as \
hard to analyse in general \[LongDash] so the numbers here are exact error \
rates for a stated protocol, not fault-tolerance proofs.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"39f2334d-24de-3dcb-6f81-ab174d688711"],

Cell["What is exact, and what is not", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1ec600b7-0050-8550-46fd-99f1b1eaefba"],

Cell["\<\
Five limits are worth stating plainly, because a result that looks exact and \
is not is worse than an estimate.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"33bfe66e-cd59-d601-6144-f84be4edbd6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Enumeration is capped.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The code-capacity route walks all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["4", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a3ee8c1-8740-e1ad-1bc5-01ab32fab3f7"],
 " errors, so it is bounded by ",
 Cell[BoxData["$QECExactEnumerationLimit"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33885b0f-111a-0c54-6188-5369a0af56be"],
 ", which is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["4", "10"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c9080a8-67dd-9047-04af-19f21269e2ad"],
 " by default. The nine-qubit Shor code takes about a second; past ten \
qubits, pass a sample count instead and get an estimate with error bars you \
control."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2abc9d06-0494-496b-5a43-1560ad211bb1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The exact circuit-level route is capped by its state space, not \
its fault count.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Folding locations into a distribution over effects costs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ")"}], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", "2", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43e301a0-76bb-1057-7190-980a034e62bd"],
 " per step, bounded by ",
 Cell[BoxData["$QECExactDetectorLimit"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ae06f2b-7109-3ba5-4a9f-877500bd898f"],
 ". That grows in the ",
 StyleBox["rounds", "TI"],
 ", so the Steane code is exact at one round and must be sampled at three. \
Sampling draws the true channels, not the independent-mechanism approximation \
attached to the detector model's rows, so the sampled number is not the \
weaker answer \[LongDash] only the slower-converging one."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0856a555-3f58-6085-386d-3d1fbaed32ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The decoder is chosen at a probe rate.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Maximum likelihood needs to compare probabilities, and with a symbolic \
rate there is nothing to compare. The argmax is therefore resolved at a small \
fixed rate, ",
 Cell[BoxData["$QECDecoderProbeRate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71eecbe3-9be0-9ba6-2795-e2cd1d9ae98c"],
 ". Once chosen the decoder is a fixed function, and the polynomial reported \
for it is exact at every p \[LongDash] but it is the polynomial for ",
 StyleBox["that", "TI"],
 " decoder, not for a decoder retuned at each p."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"59070895-187c-42ea-0f3c-a1df99091030"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The circuit-level decoder is minimum weight over fault subsets, up \
to a reach.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " It is exact at low weight and explodes combinatorially past it, so it \
stops and says so at ",
 Cell[BoxData["$QECDecoderSubsetLimit"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "189fe470-6cd8-7cf4-48a4-fe3a056d46de"],
 ". A matching decoder plugs in at the detector model and returns the same \
kind of answer; that is roadmap work, not a gap in the model."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04ed2843-d86c-272a-2c92-c22cd91e8a70"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The default extraction circuit is not fault tolerant, and is not \
claimed to be.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Its ancillas are bare rather than verified, which is what produces the \
hook errors measured above. That is an honest property of the circuit rather \
than an approximation: the rate reported is the true rate ",
 StyleBox["for this circuit", "TI"],
 ", and \[Section]12.1.1 is where to read what it costs. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Extraction\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Transversal\>\""}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d9e217-b7c7-416b-20e6-0450c27213b1"],
 " replaces it with one that is \[LongDash] conditionally: the rate it \
returns is post-selected on the cat checks accepting, and carries its \
acceptance, and the cat preparation itself is still the non-fault-tolerant \
chain of \[Section]12.1.3 rather than a chapter-13 gadget."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29221b72-bc55-8ef4-58d1-933c35e1d4de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Zero idle noise is the default, and it is the one optimistic \
assumption left.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Idling is now modelled rather than missing: the schedule is recovered from \
the instruction list by ASAP list scheduling, a qubit no instruction of a \
time step touches is waiting, and each such slot carries its three Paulis. \
But ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Idle\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41172bde-c012-830e-772c-c29bf1a4ee54"],
 " still ",
 StyleBox["defaults", "TI"],
 " to zero, and every circuit-level number in this note is computed at that \
default. Generators are extracted sequentially, so the circuit waits more \
than a parallel one would, not less; \[Section]15.5.1 quantifies the storage \
rate that serialisation multiplies, and \[Section]15.5.2 says an ill-defined \
time step is to be defined and its padding charged, never dropped. Set ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Idle\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3dd84232-0c35-660d-6bf8-647ca5c04d57"],
 " and the numbers get worse, in the direction this circuit is already \
weakest."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5558c8fc-3d33-9e90-0367-e1a6b4c7e4fa"],

Cell["How this is checked", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"53291d47-a111-bd44-02d6-9520d0a507ae"],

Cell["\<\
Nothing above is trusted because the package computed it. Every fast routine \
is cross-checked against a slow, obvious one, and the checks run as a suite \
of 593 tests.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14460f59-6b0f-818e-3c7d-a7030ebbd3d4"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "6afe19ed-5a5e-331e-1a85-90b75fe89e64"], Cell["What", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"142f588d-e120-bc70-3dd5-51d690da075a"],
     Cell["Checked against", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"029948d8-232c-2201-32a7-618256d9716b"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4b1b5b6f-b43d-594b-7939-53493dc82b91"], Cell[
    "Pauli algebra, products and phases", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "32f703b9-71e1-95eb-628c-9ae30795ff31"], Cell[TextData[{
     "Dense ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["2", 
         StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[Cross]", 
        SuperscriptBox["2", 
         StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "0c860bbc-8d1f-f590-34bd-a2e624abdffa"],
     " matrices built from scratch"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1bab88a0-6539-d521-49a8-210a0ccdbc0b"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "74b37722-3fdc-1a4f-1c41-6e8cba696895"], Cell[
    "Row layout", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "31781dc2-1028-33d4-6707-94aca1c2813e"], Cell[
    "The engine's own tableau, row for row", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2148b02c-d62e-5336-5777-2989e3db3e1c"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "183293a6-0d60-7813-49c1-0a00a4154b79"], Cell[
    "Syndromes", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "61e1f3c1-eae0-3799-179e-eaaa8e9a9de3"], Cell[
    "Expectation values measured on an actual stabilizer state", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"20bddc2d-650e-8031-5042-d6770cb8d31b"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "7a437910-f355-55ba-2a71-715d86e03f80"], Cell[
    "Encoding circuits", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "49429438-4a3e-974e-7f71-0e626fc8fd94"], Cell[
    "The state they prepare, checked check by check", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"07e2168c-1726-1a27-2d91-8fd6a2d3690d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3540c51c-f580-c338-637f-dd59fc3aae02"], Cell[
    "Structural results", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "684f0173-fe99-1571-1874-993cfb2c7c5b"], Cell[TextData[{
     "Gottesman's published values \[LongDash] ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["X", "TI"], "_"], "\[LongEqual]", 
        StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["X", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "6e32c5a8-aee9-5273-17c1-dcf5ca9c2159"],
     ", the ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"4", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
      "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "607492e2-157b-ba0c-100b-0bcc9c0f0956"],
     " generators"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"7781757c-388d-abb9-1dbf-6d26b939f983"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "566e7348-207a-dc95-7e16-6b12510ca6ff"], Cell[
    "CSS and concatenation", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "39672ae7-82f4-b353-6f1c-c3c1368601b9"], Cell["\<\
The textbook codes they must reproduce, as groups and with signs\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0c48aba4-6f27-6a39-3477-420e0ad23903"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "2f62374d-f3df-131c-5511-af16866a7e66"], Cell[
    "Noise probabilities", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "455ea632-3d4d-f0d3-7365-387cb4f9c239"], Cell[
    "The mixture the engine's channels actually return", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"1f0fb95c-030e-c889-4534-3106b6b89ad3"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "16268eae-a572-7912-3fdd-270bcc074878"], Cell[
    "Logical error rate", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "346a0e1a-2221-987e-5c69-a04457d5eb44"], Cell["\<\
A closed-form binomial tail, and an independent sampled route\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"366be24c-537a-43bb-5e68-0416660f1181"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "501b1457-1a1d-907b-0038-8e119fa9e341"], Cell[
    "The extraction circuit", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "291c68e0-f532-6cdd-5f23-81cdfcc73627"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"code", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Syndrome\>\"", ",", " ", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "]"}]], 
      "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "5c29c458-c353-7b98-05d6-de05f6e649e2"],
     ", and the circuit run as a state on the engine"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6e1a2d6a-d2ad-c32a-1639-c537e759ae70"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "6eb5612b-2266-f0f1-164b-79755710c2db"], Cell[
    "Detectors and faults", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "1f4b4965-e043-b514-4549-614e91f71c7e"], Cell["\<\
Stim's own sampler, detector by detector, over two million shots\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5bf36e21-2d79-2b6f-0980-878b440c79b5"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "6fe9f85b-1ce6-27f0-1596-f20594908dda"], Cell[
    "Circuit-level rate", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3eadea9f-7d43-757d-6652-03d974f65c47"], Cell["\<\
The code-capacity polynomial it must reduce to, and a sampled route\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"68be2dd2-eea3-f2cb-1845-c49f8b57c011"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "1279eb8d-ef8a-5dbb-4206-02d68a3f2781"], Cell[
    "Idle noise and the schedule", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6afb4307-9f81-9d1b-1a99-5b611a35e461"], Cell[TextData[{
     "The Stim export, ",
     Cell[BoxData["DEPOLARIZE1"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "2e902be9-4fb4-3e90-56af-c2b36a4684fa"],
     " line for line against the model's slots"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"46e8ad28-93a4-355d-6e97-457226569fa7"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "43090fa7-5002-8b65-7136-a60161b4d64f"], Cell[
    "Cat states", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0d6689b0-bbf9-a698-3b1d-20fa3d8d0ce2"], Cell["\<\
Every single fault propagated through the preparation, against the check set\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4ac87485-b214-a6e0-7ac8-6deec7a60cca"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "56e1d4b5-6b25-2976-7e9e-cdff0ed0785c"], Cell[
    "The encoded ancillas", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2e41722a-1026-02f0-567f-7474a1d350da"], Cell[
    "The engine: $", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6aacec8a-85e6-bbaa-1a53-05d4339009f0"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "1c51a735-fee5-6802-446e-3f7efa903b68"], Cell[
    "Fault tolerance of the gadgets", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5e54a15d-ecde-9aa9-066b-39068568e8f3"], Cell["\<\
The residual data weight over every single fault, against the bare-ancilla \
circuit measuring the same operator\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"27fb6428-ecec-27d4-4d99-7e75849e8d3e"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "51f5ca74-88a2-9d2c-078a-ec3e2954e476"], Cell["\<\
That a transversal extraction can go in a detector model at all\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1154648e-ef0b-aa2b-476c-7deb8abff971"], 
    Cell["\<\
Its effect on 200 random fault pairs, against the XOR of their rows\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4c057904-8649-af2b-743b-716e33fdf271"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "2baf9433-2e90-ebaf-5954-0e7d4b2ab9f5"], Cell[
    "That it restores the exponent", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "340e6ec8-e38f-b030-5c35-8795963b031a"], Cell["\<\
The rate at two physical rates a factor of two apart, slope read off\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"64bff79f-1679-3ebc-0c44-eed9a30d8486"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "126dc52b-3dd5-bd31-4212-dd75b461041b"], Cell[
    "That a transversal CNOT is the logical CNOT", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "28023c0b-10a3-7000-5831-b655a156436a"], Cell["\<\
Conjugating the logical operators through it, and the stabilizer group \
mapping to itself\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4f1b960d-0301-b7cd-7538-0857b6b51d17"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "268b8fe7-2cf2-fa64-4e88-26c14484c94e"], Cell[
    "That a transversal gate is the gate you think it is", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"41763b34-5a53-ec31-770d-b37e5fe7b71b"], Cell[TextData[{
     "The gate's own matrix, conjugated with the ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Z",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "5d61c4f4-c0fb-847a-0b1e-ddb1f08fef40"],
     " phase carried; the logical gate against the complex conjugate of the \
physical one"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"72fe9a0c-0c49-239f-2285-1c56a5fc71e5"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "14bcbead-0cb8-f132-3c43-37f7a532c018"], Cell[
    "That the assembled FT(C) computes C", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4a015340-38cc-91ca-7a3f-4b2ab97ee310"], Cell["\<\
The engine: the gate gadgets alone, run with no faults, must leave the blocks \
in the state the ideal circuit would\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"44807b7f-366d-41a7-6cb0-73394318138d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "56b5d630-2397-dc8b-7e4a-c87a5623a6d1"], Cell[
    "The exported circuit", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "066e8396-42fa-b64f-2e15-1ad0768c1c95"], Cell[
    "PyMatching, which decodes it unchanged", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0fee4e15-659c-ade9-3596-605f0c2ef733"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"6f99faa1-7599-adaa-15a6-f30b7c2df7f0"],

Cell["\<\
The habit is worth keeping when extending the layer: a result checked only \
against the code that produced it is not checked.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c80f068-193e-1d5a-14bf-ea3298cb67a0"],

